WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:12.170
69. Magic Realism. Literature is a huge concept. In order to talk about it more

2
00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:16.490
meaningfully, we break it down into styles, groups of writing that use

3
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:24.150
similar effects, themes, or tactics. One of these styles is magic realism. Magic

4
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:29.330
realism in literature comes from South America. The Colombian writer Gabriel

5
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:35.090
Garcia Marquez is one writer very closely associated with the term. But

6
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:41.210
magic realism was actually first used by a German art critic in 1925 to talk

7
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:46.530
about a style of painting. That style of painting, putting magical objects or

8
00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.930
concepts in a real world, had the same effect as magic realism in literature.

9
00:00:51.930 --> 00:01:00.170
However, magic realism wasn't used as a literary term until 1955. Magic realism

10
00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:07.010
is not fantasy. Instead, it is serious realistic fiction that includes magical

11
00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:12.410
or supernatural elements in a real normal setting. The magical elements in

12
00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.850
that setting are not seen as magic. They're just part of a world that looks

13
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.890
like ours but is slightly different. Magic realism uses these magic elements

14
00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:30.970
to help tell very real, not fantastic, stories. In order for magic realism to

15
00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:35.690
work, the reader must accept that these magic elements are not necessarily

16
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:42.990
surprising but just part of the world of the story. Magic realism is a complicated

17
00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:48.430
idea. Some critics say the term is out-of-date now and want a new, more

18
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:53.710
accurate one. Some critics have never liked the term and say it contributes to

19
00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.830
racism. Instead of letting this type of Latin American writing simply join

20
00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:06.230
literature, a new genre was created to avoid taking it seriously. Magic realism

21
00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:10.950
has played a very important role in modern literature. What it will do in the

22
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:16.630
future is today's question. Will it continue to tell serious stories or will

23
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:21.070
it merge with light fiction and fantasy?
